From f29ef33258625d1562e679d4e6917ef4ab38284c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erhan Bilgili <erhan.bilgili@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 07:42:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Avoid scaling configure sizes twice.

Since the fractional scaling rework, xdg configure rectangles are stored
in window coordinates when the event is received. Do not convert the
already mapped size again when applying the raw window position.

This avoids oversized maximized, tiled or fullscreen windows on
fractional scale outputs.

(cherry picked from commit f29ef33258625d1562e679d4e6917ef4ab38284c)

Source: https://github.com/nanomatters/wine-salkim/commit/f29ef33258625d1562e679d4e6917ef4ab38284c
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
index 17152af6cae..9e8a1e85595 100644
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -1010,8 +1010,8 @@ static void wayland_configure_window(HWND hwnd)
         flags |= SWP_NOSIZE;
     }
 
-    wayland_surface_coords_to_window(surface, width, height,
-                                     &window_width, &window_height);
+    window_width = width;
+    window_height = height;
     offset_x = ((surface->window.rect.left - surface->window.window_rect.left) +
                 (surface->window.window_rect.right - surface->window.rect.right));
     offset_y = ((surface->window.rect.top - surface->window.window_rect.top) +
-- 
2.55.0

